  provenance: "All AUTHORED (RH Aviator W45; no public source describes a generic
    line pilot), tuned headless against slice 3a's pass criteria (ROADMAP, fixed
    before tuning). Hands: guidanceGain (2, the classic value of the L1 path-following
    law, Park, Deyst and How, AIAA 2004-4900, PUBLIC method), maxBankDeg, rollRatePerBankDeg,
    climbDegPerM, maxClimbDeg, maxDiveDeg, gPerPathDeg, maxG (below the F/A-18E's
    7.5 G limit: a line pilot does not fly at the limit), throttlePerKt, throttleTrim,
    throttleIntegralPerKtS, speedBrakeOverKt. Ground guard: floorAglM (100 m, about
    330 ft), guardLookAheadS, guardClimbDeg, guardMaxBankDeg. Route: leadInM, carrotM,
    carrotTurnRadii, throughM, minRunM, captureDeg, captureFraction, cruiseKt, bandMarginKt.
    After the course: holdAltitudeM (3,000 ft), holdKt. Fingertip (W40): slotRightM
    (40 m, about three of the F/A-18E's 13.6 m wingspans, centre to centre), slotBackM,
    slotUpM, slotLookAheadM, slotGainPerS, joinDecelMps2 (below what an F/A-18E at
    idle loses near 400 kt, about 2.3 m/s\xB2 in slice 3b's trace, so the plan is
    flyable), joinOvertakeKt, slotOvertakeKt, joinMinKt, inSlotM, inSlotClosureKt,
    lostSlotM, slotSpeedLead, slotSpeedBrakeOverKt, slotClimbDegPerM, slotGPerPathDeg,
    slotRotationShare (the last three picked by FormationTests.Sweep, a grid on the
    fixed hold scenario: 0.5 G per degree sits 1.6 times inside where the hold rings,
    at 0.6 it degrades and at 0.8 it diverges). Going home (W41, W47; the shape as
    the U.S. Navy publicly describes its overhead break, the numbers fitted): initialM,
    initialCaptureM, initialKt, breakAlongM, breakHeightM (800 ft), breakKt, downwindOffsetM,
    downwindHeightM (600 ft), finalTurnAlongM, approachKt (145 kt, as Air Wing's
    landing test), gearKt, patternBankDeg, patternGPerPathDeg, patternMaxDiveDeg,
    patternFloorAglM, glidePathDeg, touchdownM, flareHeightM, flarePathDeg, finalCarrotM,
    rolloutPedalPerM, rolloutPedalPerDeg, bingoFlightTimeS (a STAND-IN for bingo
    fuel until fuel burn exists; 0 = never). The fight (Pilot L1, W38, W45; a game's
    skill numbers, AUTHORED, not any real pilot's or air force's): fieldOfViewDeg,
    reactionDelayS, memoryS, visualRangeM, cornerKt, leadS, lagS, lagRangeM, overshootClosureKt,
    lagSlowKt, threatRangeM, threatConeDeg, fightFloorM, clearRangeM, slowKt (energy
    sense; 0 = none), turnMatch, rangeKtPerM, attackRangeM, chaseOverKt (range control;
    0 = none), avoidM, avoidS (collision avoidance); joinAvoidM (25 m, inside the
    40 m slot spacing: a join with no fight avoids too, after a survey of four-ship
    joins found crossed joins meeting at 0 m). Trigger discipline (Gunnery K6): gunRangeM
    900, triggerMils 12 (a burst that would pass within 12 mils of where the target
    will be; AUTHORED). Missile discipline (Air Wing W65, A16; SIX 2026-10-29: rookies
    early, aces close): missileRangeM 3500 (launch with the seeker locked on its
    target inside 3.5 km, one at a time; AUTHORED). Rookie, from the line pilot (AUTHORED):
    maxG 4.5, maxBankDeg 60, fieldOfViewDeg 90, reactionDelayS 1.2, memoryS 4, visualRangeM
    6000, cornerKt 380 (fights too fast), leadS 0 and lagS 0 (pure pursuit only),
    threatRangeM 1000, slowKt 0 (no energy sense), turnMatch 0, rangeKtPerM 0 (no
    range control), gunRangeM 1400 and triggerMils 30 (sprays: long and wide), missileRangeM
    5000 (launches as soon as it locks)."
